# ===== The entire autonomous_agency/ tree: private, never tracked =====
# Operator directive 2026-09-28: autonomous_agency/ in its COMPLETENESS is
# private working material. Not just the generated output, the whole
# directory. Overrides the earlier name-based rules, which only covered the
# loop's output and deliberately left the source trackable.
#
# What this drops from tracking: 26 tracked files.
#   20 source:  config.py, settings.py, backtester.py, broker.py,
#               perpetual_loop.py, strategy_factory.py, mutation_engine.py,
#               evolution_engine.py, mutant_factory.py, mssql_store.py,
#               sweep.py, concept_vocab_ext.py, bulk_1m.py,
#               scripts/batch_backtest.py, ... + README.md
#    3 source:  strategies/base.py, strategies/concepts.py,
#               strategies/disjoint_gate.py  (imported by 15 modules)
#    3 loop output:  the hand-written crossover_* entries
#
# CONSEQUENCE, stated plainly: a clone of this repo will NOT contain
# autonomous_agency/. The code does not travel with the repo. The files stay
# on this machine. That is what was asked for.
#
# The leading slash anchors the rule to the repo root, so a nested copy is
# not silently left covered by accident.
/autonomous_agency/

# dontcommit.py: local credentials module (RC3) — never tracked
dependencies/backtrader/dontcommit.py
dontcommit.py
